From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 15:55:24 +0000
Subject: MIPS: intel-mips: set NR_CPUS=4 in grx500_defconfig

The GRX350's interAptiv cluster is 2 cores x 2 VPEs, i.e. 4 logical
CPUs. The FRITZ!Box 7560 board DTS added by this series declares all
four, and the OpenWrt overlay for this target already ships
CONFIG_NR_CPUS=4, so raise the in-tree defconfig to match the hardware
topology instead of describing half of it.

This is not an SMP enablement. Boot remains effectively uniprocessor:
smp-cps self-disables on this platform, because the CPS vector
allocation is skipped under the CONFIG_INTEL_MIPS guard in
cps_smp_setup() so core_entry_reg stays zero and cps_prepare_cpus()
bails out with "core_entry address unsuitable"; the shipped cmdline
also carries nosmp. Secondary bring-up is barred on this SoC in the
first place, as the CM2 reset vector for a secondary core cannot reach
RAM above PHYS_OFFSET through CKSEG1.

What the value does buy is correctness for anything sized off NR_CPUS.
Nothing in the tree should be, but getting the topology right removes a
class of latent mis-sizing at zero runtime cost.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig b/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
index 9dd7ba8e1f74..c81e5195923f 100644
--- a/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/configs/grx500_defconfig
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@ CONFIG_SCHED_SMT=y
 # CONFIG_MIPS_MT_FPAFF is not set
 CONFIG_MIPS_CPS=y
 CONFIG_DEFAULT_MMAP_MIN_ADDR=65536
-CONFIG_NR_CPUS=2
+CONFIG_NR_CPUS=4
 CONFIG_HZ_100=y
 # CONFIG_SECCOMP is not set
 # CONFIG_LOCALVERSION_AUTO is not set
